      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Yazoo and Mississippi Valley Railroad spurred Benoit’s growth, ferrying cotton from surrounding plantations into the Delta’s trade network.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/benoit_mississippi",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Covering about one square mile, Benoit remains a quiet farming community focused on cotton and soybeans, echoing its Delta heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/benoit_mississippi",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Settlement in the area began after the 1830 Treaty of Dancing Rabbit Creek, which opened the land for European‑American settlers and led to Bolivar County’s 1836 creation.",
